---
// /en/therapy/ (переработка 2026-07-12): структура сверена с боевой RU /therapy/
// (hero с фото, pullquote, «in session you can», FAQ по логике продаж).
// EN-отличия: онлайн-only, 60 €, CET, интро-звонок 30 минут, префиллы на английском.
import Page from '../../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { site } from '../../../data/site';
---

<Page
  title="Individual Therapy in English · Valeriy Karasaev"
  description="How therapy works: first session, 50-minute online format, 60 € per session, confidentiality, FAQ. Gestalt therapist and executive coach, in practice since 2014."
  lang="en"
  wide={true}
  translation="/therapy/"
>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <div class="p-hero" style="margin: 0 -20px;">
    <div class="p-hero-in">
      <div class="p-hero-txt">
        <div class="kicker">Individual Therapy</div>
        <h1>When handling it alone got too expensive</h1>
        <p class="lead" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
          Everything looks fine on paper - and feels empty inside. You understand everything -
          and still don't move. If this sounds familiar, you are in the right place.
        </p>
        <div class="btn-group" style="justify-content: flex-start; margin: 0;">
          <a href={site.en.telegramSession} class="btn btn-primary">Book a first session</a>
          <a href={site.en.telegramQuestion} class="btn btn-outline">Ask a question</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="p-hero-photo">
        <img src="/images/photo/therapy-hero.jpg" alt="Valeriy Karasaev" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="shell content-narrow" style="margin-top: 44px;">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        People usually come to me at times of crisis and transition: burnout, divorce, relocation,
        job loss, loss of meaning, hard decisions. These are the moments when life is changing -
        and you need a reliable second person next to you, to untangle things and find new ground.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Pullquote -->
    <div class="pullquote">
      <p>«Therapy begins when you can no longer live a life that isn't yours».</p>
      <div class="attr">Valeriy Karasaev</div>
    </div>

    <!-- First session -->
    <div class="meta-line"><span class="meta-num">01</span><span class="meta-label">The first session</span></div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The first session is an introduction. We look at what brings you, I explain how I work,
        and you decide whether to continue. No commitments beyond paying for one session.
        Before that, we can have a free 30-minute intro call - to meet, ask questions
        and see whether we click.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- How we work -->
    <div class="meta-line"><span class="meta-num">02</span><span class="meta-label">How we work</span></div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        In short - in three layers. We look at what is happening with you right now: in feelings,
        in the body, in contact. We notice the scripts that have been repeating for years.
        And when it is time to act, we add structure and concrete steps. Whatever you need now -
        that is what we work with.
      </p>
      <p>
        Therapy is a dialogue. I don't hand out advice: my role is to be next to you,
        not to drag you behind me. Only then do your decisions become truly yours -
        and integrate as part of your life.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Format and fees -->
    <div class="meta-line"><span class="meta-num">03</span><span class="meta-label">Format and fees</span></div>
    <div class="spec">
      <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">Session</span><span class="spec-val">50 minutes · online, camera on</span></div>
      <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">Fee</span><span class="spec-val">{site.session.priceEur} per session</span></div>
      <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">Schedule</span><span class="spec-val">{site.en.schedule}</span></div>
      <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">Platforms</span><span class="spec-val">Google Meet / Zoom</span></div>
      <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">Payment</span><span class="spec-val">PayPal · IBAN · card</span></div>
      <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">Languages</span><span class="spec-val">English · Russian</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Full working agreements - cancellations, rescheduling, confidentiality, boundaries -
        are collected in one document:
        <a href="/docs/working-rules-en.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Working Rules (PDF)</a>.
        The essentials, in plain language: <a href="/en/principles/">Working Principles</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- In session you can -->
    <div class="meta-line"><span class="meta-num">04</span><span class="meta-label">In session you can</span></div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Cry and laugh. Swear. Talk about sex, money and envy. Be angry - including at me.
        Be unsuccessful, confused and humanly vulnerable. Say the things you have never told anyone.
        Stay silent when there are no words yet. You don't have to be convenient here -
        you have to be real.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <div id="faq" class="meta-line"><span class="meta-num">05</span><span class="meta-label">FAQ</span></div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>What do people come to you with most often?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">Burnout and chronic stress. Loss of meaning. Divorce and separation. Expat life. Repeating relationship patterns. Leadership loneliness. Career transitions. Men's topics: vulnerability, aggression, self-worth. And much more. This is not a closed list - if in doubt, write to me.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What if I don't know my "request"? Do I need to prepare?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">No preparation needed. Come as you are - tired, confused, angry, without formulations. «I want to figure things out» and «something is off, I don't know what» are already a good start. Figuring out what is going on is part of the work, and we do it together.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Therapy or coaching - which one do I need?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">Coaching is about goals and steps: where am I going and how do I get there. Therapy is about what keeps repeating and getting in the way: feelings, scripts, relationships. I am a certified coach and a Gestalt therapist, so we can work in the layer you need - and switch when it makes sense.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How often do we meet, and how many sessions will I need?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">Usually once a week. It can be more or less often - regularity depends on your request, state and possibilities, and we discuss it openly. As for numbers: short-term focused work - blocks of 5-10 sessions; an acute crisis - sometimes 10-20; deep work with patterns - from half a year. We review regularly whether we are heading the right way.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can a session be longer?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">Yes. A standard session is 50 minutes. We can work for 80 or 100 minutes - let's discuss what fits your task.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Why book several sessions in advance?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">Effective work is regular. Your chosen time slot is reserved for you: the work builds best in the same place, at the same time, on the same day.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does online therapy actually work?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">Yes. Most of my practice is online and it works as well as in-person meetings. You need a private space, stable internet and your camera on.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What don't you work with?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">I work with adults 18+. I don't work with children and teenagers, chemical addictions or severe psychiatric conditions - in those cases I can recommend a psychiatrist.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is it confidential?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">Yes. Everything said in sessions stays between us. Two exceptions: supervision (discussing the work without names or identifying details - a professional standard) and a direct threat to life. Details are in the working rules.</div>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div class="prose" style="margin-top: 26px;">
      <p>
        Not sure individual therapy is what you need? There is also an English-speaking
        therapy group - <a href="/en/groups/work-ambition/">«Work, People, Ambition»</a>.
        Or simply <a href={site.en.telegramFreeCall}>book a free 30-minute call</a> -
        we will figure it out together.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Page>
